<%# The Freeze button, or the badge that replaces it once frozen (R9).
    Rendered by all four chrome partials so the surfaces cannot drift, and by
    Admin::Freezing when it re-renders that chrome into a Turbo Stream.

    Hidden entirely when there is nothing to freeze (R15) — no pools drawn, no
    bracket generated, or a bracket-only category's absent pool phase.

    Only the unfreeze side confirms (R14): freezing is harmless and reversible,
    unfreezing re-opens the tools that destroy recorded work.

    The state is read through FreezeHelper rather than into template locals:
    erb_lint lints each ERB tag on its own, so a local read in a later tag
    looks useless and the pre-commit autocorrect deletes it. %>
<% if freeze_freezable?(category, flag) %>
  <span class="freeze-control">
    <% if freeze_frozen_at(category, flag) %>
      <span class="freeze-control__badge freeze-control__badge--frozen">
        <%= t("admin.freezes.badge", at: l(freeze_frozen_at(category, flag), format: :short)) %>
      </span>
      <%= button_to t("admin.freezes.unfreeze.#{flag}"), freeze_path(category, flag),
            method: :delete, class: "freeze-control__button",
            form: {data: {turbo_confirm: t("admin.freezes.unfreeze_confirm.#{flag}")}} %>
    <% else %>
      <%= button_to t("admin.freezes.freeze.#{flag}"), freeze_path(category, flag),
            method: :post, class: "freeze-control__button" %>
    <% end %>
  </span>
<% end %>
